---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---
<Layout title="Privacy" description="Morningwit keeps your puzzle progress in your own browser and shows ads from Adsterra. This page says what is stored, what the ads do and how to opt out." noindex>
	<div class="wrap-narrow prose">
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p><em>Last updated September 30, 2026.</em></p>

		<h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
		<p>
			To remember your boards, timer preference, colour theme, streaks, the last valid word box you typed and your ad choice, Morningwit uses your browser's local storage. That data lives on your device.
			It is not sent to us. Clearing site data in your browser removes it.
		</p>

		<h2>What we collect</h2>
		<p>
			We do not ask for an account, a name or an email address to play. We do not run analytics.
			Like any website, our host may keep standard server logs, such as request time and IP address, for security and to keep the site running.
		</p>

		<h2>Advertising</h2>
		<p>
			Morningwit shows ads served by Adsterra. They appear below the puzzles and inside guides, never on a board. Adsterra and its demand partners may set cookies or use similar identifiers to serve and measure ads, including interest-based ads. They receive your IP address and details about your browser and device.
			What they do with that is described in the <a href="https://adsterra.com/privacy-policy/">Adsterra privacy policy</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Your choices about ads</h2>
		<p>
			If your browser's time zone is in Europe, which we use as a rough stand-in for the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, we ask before loading ads, and nothing from Adsterra loads until you allow it. Elsewhere ads load by default.
			If your browser sends a <a href="https://globalprivacycontrol.org/">Global Privacy Control</a> signal, we treat it as a no. A choice you make is stored in your browser, and you can change it any time with the Ad choices link at the bottom of every page.
		</p>
		<p>
			You can also use your browser's tracking controls or an ad blocker. The <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.com/">Your Online Choices</a> site explains how to opt out of interest-based ads in Europe.
		</p>

		<h2>Cookies</h2>
		<p>Morningwit does not set cookies of its own. Once ads load, Adsterra and its partners may set theirs.</p>

		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>If this changes, for example if analytics are added later, this page will be updated first and will say so plainly.</p>

		<h2>Questions</h2>
		<p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
